 \section{Conclusion}
 \label{sec:conclusion}
 
-Geometry-control allocation changes generated-view agreement, but its effects depend on the tested interface, protocol and endpoint. The matched 300-object study shows that C3's gain over fixed low combines increased strength with timing; equal-budget fixed mean and late-high outperform the historical middle window. Native MV-Adapter studies do not detect the primary middle-window advantage, while some secondary image effects are small but measurable. Actual baking yields a limited late-high benefit on ten compatible GeoTex objects and no detected LPIPS benefit on a separate twenty-object GSO cohort. Method rankings are broadly associated across image and baked evaluation, yet their preferred operating points often differ. Competitive controls and application-level evaluation are therefore necessary when choosing a setting within a deployed pipeline. The results do not identify a universally preferred schedule or establish faithful material reproduction.
+Geometry-control allocation changes generated-view agreement, but its effects depend on the tested interface, protocol and endpoint. The matched 300-object study shows that C3's gain over fixed low combines increased strength with timing; equal-budget fixed mean and late-high outperform the historical middle window. Native MV-Adapter studies do not detect the primary middle-window advantage, while some secondary image effects are small but measurable. Actual baking yields a limited late-high benefit on ten compatible GeoTex objects and no detected LPIPS benefit on a separate twenty-object GSO cohort. Method rankings are broadly associated across image and baked evaluation, yet their preferred operating points often differ. The original middle-versus-early/late-average contrast does not detect a gain. A separately retrained historical cohort also demonstrates opposite full-frame and foreground PSNR directions. Competitive controls, explicitly named image regions and application-level evaluation are therefore necessary when choosing a setting within a deployed pipeline. The results do not identify a universally preferred schedule or establish faithful material reproduction.
 
